        "label": "Centrosome and centrioles",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Centrioles",
        "lines": [
          "A centrosome contains two cylindrical",
          "structures called centrioles, lying at right",
          "angles to each other.",
          "When a centriole is cut across, the pattern",
          "seen in the section is called the cartwheel."
        ],
        "why": "The cartwheel is what a transverse section of a centriole looks like, so the answer has to begin by saying that a centriole is a cylinder seen end on.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that a centrosome has one centriole. It has two.",
          "Writing that the two centrioles lie parallel. They lie at right angles."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Two cylinders at right angles make one centrosome; cut one across and the cartwheel appears.",
        "margin_note": "Two centrioles at right angles is the opening mark."
